# SNOWFLOW

Real-time procedural snow demo. **WebGPU only** (Babylon.js + hand-written WGSL). No WebGL fallback. No third-party textures, meshes, HDRIs, or animation clips — everything is generated on the GPU at load (or lofted from numeric tables).

## Layout

```
src/main.js          entry + frame orchestration (order is load-bearing)
src/core/            settings, input, camera, perf, loading, gpuUtil
src/terrain/         heightfield, clipmap, deformation state buffer
src/render/          sky/IBL, shadow cascades, depth prepass
src/character/       skeleton, procedural mesh, cloth, snow contact
src/vfx/             spray particles, surf wake
src/spells/          five spells, shared water body, light pool
src/post/            TAA, bloom, shafts, DoF, SSR, tonemap
src/ui/              F1 settings / perf overlay
src/shaders/         WGSL sources; lib/ = shared #includes
```

## Hard constraints

- **No allocation in the render loop.** Pre-size buffers/typed arrays at construction; write in place. Module-scope scratch (`_vel`, `_aim`) is the pattern — never `new` per frame.
- **Warm up behind the loading screen.** Every material / procedural texture / pipeline must `warmUp()` / `whenReady()` before the first interactive frame. A first cast must not compile mid-frame.
- **Keep systems modular.** New features go in their domain folder. Do not dump logic into `main.js` or grow unrelated modules. Wire in `main.js` only for construction order and per-frame call order.
- **Shared snow state.** Feet, wake, and spells all write deformation through `DeformationField.brush()`. Lit surfaces read the same spell light pool (`SpellLights` / `#include<snowSpellLights>`).
- **Rendering groups:** 0 = sky, 1 = opaque scene, 2 = alpha (water, spray). Depth auto-clear between groups is disabled on purpose.
- Prefer lean, readable changes. Do not add fallbacks, catch-alls, or speculative branches.

## Run

```bash
npm install && npm run dev   # http://localhost:5173
```
